<span id="A6.SS19.SSS2.2" class="ltx_inline-block fas fa-edit" aria-hidden="true">
</span>  framesI_tweets23 task</h4>

<div id="A6.SS19.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A6.I52" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I52.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I52.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I52.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I52.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Task description:</span> General frame detection: whether a tweet contains a set of two opposing frames ("problem" and "solution"). The solution frame describes tweets framing content moderation as a solution to other issues (e.g., hate speech). The problem frame describes tweets framing content moderation as a problem on its own as well as to other issues (e.g., free speech).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I52.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
